  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 and chorus, verified against the LilyPond score on the Wikisource transcription of 'The Riverside Song Book' (1893; verse on page 60, chorus on page 61). The score prints the tune in two-part chords; the melody is the top note of each chord. The two tied sixteenths of the pickup are one eighth note ('Mine'); dotted-eighth/sixteenth rhythms and the score's rests are kept. No simplification needed. D drum: as written (range low 3 to 3), D minLayout 15. C drum: the C drum has no low 3/4, so the low figures 'Mine eyes have seen the glory', 'the grapes of wrath are stored, He hath loosed the fateful lightning', 'Glory! glory!' (first chorus line) and 'lujah! Glory! glory!' (end of the second, start of the third chorus line) are played one octave higher; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–5: Julia Ward Howe's text as printed with the tune in The Riverside Song Book (1893), pp. 36–37, from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page:The_Riverside_song_book.djvu/60 and /61). The 'Glory! glory! Hallelujah!' chorus (ending 'His truth is marching on') is sung after every verse. Per-verse notes (verseLines): in verses 2–5 the first line starts with two syllables ('I have', 'I have', 'He has', 'In the'), so the eighth-note pickup is played as two sixteenths of the same pitch, as that songbook's score shows.",
  "verified": true
}
